{
	"name": "Haute Couture",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/commodities/cloth/cloth-rolls-rgb.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Starting at 15th level, the rarity for Wondrous Items that you may transmute an enchantment from using your @UUID[Compendium.out-of-the-wilds.features.Item.SZHY7kD8nYsVYB83]{Concealed Alterations} feature increases to Very Rare.</p><p>Additionally, you gain the following benefits:</p><h2>Armored Jacket</h2><p>You are able to transmute the properties of armor into mundane clothing, turning even the most precisely tailored outfit into a protective layer. By spending 8 hours, you may transmute the properties of a suit of any armor into cloth clothing. You must have the schematic for this armor as normal, and a creature attempting to wear it must still have the relevant armor proficiency and ability score prerequisites to gain all of its benefits.</p><h2>Improved Concealment</h2><p>Your fingers are more deft than ever with a needle and thread. The amount of time it takes for you to transmute non-armor based enchantments into clothing is reduced by a number of hours equal to your Intelligence modifier. Creatures attempting to detect your Concealed Alterations via spells or other magical means must now roll their spellcasting ability check at disadvantage.</p>",
